1vfo|v|To render slow; to slacken the speed of; to retard; to delay; as, to slow a steamer. ; To go slower; -- often with up; as, the train slowed up before crossing the bridge.	o:gd,27,1~gd,27,1	d:1unm,28,4~1unm,28,4
1vfo|a|Moving a short space in a relatively long time; not swift; not quick in motion; not rapid; moderate; deliberate; as, a slow stream; a slow motion. ; Not happening in a short time; gradual; late. ; Not ready; not prompt or quick; dilatory; sluggish; as, slow of speech, and slow of tongue. ; Not hasty; not precipitate; acting with deliberation; tardy; inactive. ; Behind in time; indicating a time earlier than the true time; as, the clock or watch is slow. ; Not advancing or improving rapidly; as, the slow growth of arts and sciences. ; Heavy in wit; not alert, prompt, or spirited; wearisome; dull.	j:1fon,60,5;w08,51,3;1b56,46,6;1lwo,44,13;gd,42,3;1q4p,35,6;1wkt,29,8;1o9k,28,3;ex5,26,2;qp1,25,5~1lwo,44,13;1lmq,16,12;1wkt,29,8;1lqj,15,8;1lmu,14,8;1b56,46,6;1q4p,35,6;qp1,25,5;1qab,1,5;1fon,60,5	e:qod,34,13;10tq,30,2;1p8k,28,6;qw7,13,3;1o5i,11,8;2753,7,29;1w24,6,2;1np9,5,6;1lgp,3,4;1oar,1,9~2753,7,29;qod,34,13;1oar,1,9;1o5i,11,8;1np9,5,6;1p8k,28,6;1lgp,3,4;qw7,13,3;10tq,30,2;1w24,6,2
